$ muster -h
Run a project's dev processes in the background, and control them from any shell

Usage: muster [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Processes:
  ps            List this project's processes
  up            Start the processes that autostart
  down          Stop every process
  start         Start a process
  stop          Stop a process
  restart       Restart a process
  pause         Suspend a process, leaving it alive
  resume        Resume a paused process
  kill          Kill a process at once
  wait          Wait until a process is ready or prints a line
  logs          Print or follow a process's log
  attach        Show a process in this terminal and type into it
  open          Show a process in a new terminal pane beside this one
  run           Add a command, start it and attach to it

Stack:
  add           Add a process to this project
  set           Change a process's definition
  rm            Remove processes from this project
  import        Load processes from a stack file
  export        Write this project's processes to a stack file
  init          Detect processes in this folder and add them
  projects      List and manage registered projects

Agents and coordination:
  mcp           Serve muster to an agent over MCP
  note          Read or write shared notes
  todo          List or manage shared todos
  kv            Read or write shared key-value state
  lock          List agents' locks, or release one
  coordination  Export or restore the shared coordination state
  notices       Show agents' stack edits and recent failures

Setup:
  config        Show or change muster's settings
  shell-init    Print the shell hook that starts projects you enter
  completions   Print the shell hook that enables completions
  doctor        Check muster's setup for problems
  service       Show or stop the muster service

Options:
  -p, --project <PROJECT>  The project to act on, by name or folder
  -h, --help               Print help
  -V, --version            Print version

Exit codes and JSON output: https://github.com/sagoez/muster/blob/main/docs/reference.md


$ muster ps -h
List this project's processes

Usage: muster ps [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --all                List every project the muster service has loaded
  -p, --project <PROJECT>  The project to act on, by name or folder
      --commands           Add a COMMAND column with each process's stored command, so an edit made by an agent shows
      --json               Print the result as JSON
  -h, --help               Print help (see more with '--help')


$ muster up -h
Start the processes that autostart

Usage: muster up [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json               Print the result as JSON
  -p, --project <PROJECT>  The project to act on, by name or folder
  -h, --help               Print help


