$ muster start -h
Start a process

Usage: muster start [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]  The process, as `muster ps` lists it; quote a name with spaces. Chosen from a list at a terminal when absent

Options:
      --json                Print the result as JSON
  -p, --project <PROJECT>   The project to act on, by name or folder
      --wait                Wait until its new run passes its readiness check, or runs when it has none
      --timeout <DURATION>  With --wait, the longest to wait, such as 60s; unbounded when absent
  -h, --help                Print help


