$ muster wait -h
Wait until a process is ready or prints a line

Usage: muster wait [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]  The process, as `muster ps` lists it; quote a name with spaces. Chosen from a list at a terminal when absent

Options:
      --log <TEXT>          Wait for an output line containing this text
  -p, --project <PROJECT>   The project to act on, by name or folder
      --regex               Read --log as a regular expression
      --port <PORT>         Wait until a TCP connection to this localhost port succeeds
      --http <URL>          Wait until this localhost URL answers below 500
      --status <CODE>       With --http, the status to wait for instead
      --state <STATE>       Wait for a lifecycle state; `stopped` means not running at all [possible values: running, paused, exited, crashed, restarting, stopped]
      --timeout <DURATION>  The longest to wait, such as 60s; unbounded when absent
      --since <CURSOR>      Count output after this cursor, from an earlier wait's result, as well as output after the command started
      --json                Print the result as JSON
  -h, --help                Print help (see more with '--help')


