$ muster export -h
Write this project's processes to a stack file

Usage: muster export [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]  The file to write; `-` prints it. Defaults to muster.yml in the project's folder

Options:
      --force              Overwrite an existing file
  -p, --project <PROJECT>  The project to act on, by name or folder
      --with-env           Write environment values too; without it each variable is written with no value, to be filled in before importing
      --json               Print the result as JSON
  -h, --help               Print help


$ muster import -h
Load processes from a stack file

Usage: muster import [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]  The file to read; `-` reads stdin. Defaults to muster.yml in the project's folder

Options:
      --merge              Replace same-named processes and keep the others
  -p, --project <PROJECT>  The project to act on, by name or folder
      --replace            Make the project's processes exactly the file's, stopping and removing the others
      --dry-run            Print what would change and change nothing
      --json               Print the result as JSON
  -h, --help               Print help (see more with '--help')


