$ muster completions -h
Print the shell hook that enables completions

Usage: muster completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>  Shell to print the hook for [possible values: bash, zsh, fish, elvish, powershell]

Options:
  -p, --project <PROJECT>  The project to act on, by name or folder
  -h, --help               Print help


$ muster shell-init -h
Print the shell hook that starts projects you enter

Usage: muster shell-init [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>  Shell to print the hook for [possible values: bash, zsh, fish]

Options:
  -p, --project <PROJECT>  The project to act on, by name or folder
  -h, --help               Print help (see more with '--help')
